                        <provenance type="#rejected"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_1008">Burton
                                Latimer, Northamptonshire. Parish church</orgName>
                            <p>This attribution was rejected in the second edition of Medieval
                                Libraries of Great Britain (1964), which did not change in the
                                Supplement (1987). The corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great
                                Britain index card records the following information, which was
                                deemed unsatisfactory for an attribution:</p><p> 10 leaves only,
                                found by Reverend R. M. Serjeantson <q>sewn together to form the
                                    cover of a book of churchwardens' accounts dating from 1559</q>.
                                Compare <title>Transactions of St Paul's Ecclesiological
                                    Society</title> V (1905), 251ff.</p></provenance>
                        <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">In 1995, Burton Latimer Parish church
                            petitioned the Constitory Court of the Diocese of Peterborough for
                            permission to sell the missal leaves. However, it was ultimately agreed
                            that the leaves would be deposited in the County Record
                            Office.</provenance>
                    </history>
